WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.733 --> 00:00:01.967
-Hey, everyone.

00:00:01.967 --> 00:00:03.903
This past weekend,
we lost an absolute legend.

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:06.005
TV host and
our good friend Regis Philbin

00:00:06.005 --> 00:00:08.474
passed away at 88 years old.

00:00:08.474 --> 00:00:11.077
Regis got his start
as an NBC page

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:12.211
at "The Tonight Show,"
right here,

00:00:12.211 --> 00:00:14.180
when Steve Allen was the host.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:16.716
But the big break for him
was in 1967,

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:18.651
when he became famous
as the sidekick

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:21.421
on "The Joey Bishop Show."

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:23.556
He could do everything.
He could sing.

00:00:23.556 --> 00:00:26.725
He was funny.
He was really funny.

00:00:26.725 --> 00:00:28.494
He was an entertainer.

00:00:28.494 --> 00:00:31.531
He always was game
to do a bit or dress up.

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:33.299
He would do anything
for a laugh.

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:35.768
I loved him.
My grandparents loved him.

00:00:35.768 --> 00:00:37.971
They introduced me.
My mom and dad loved him.

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:39.605
Between his early career
and his time on

00:00:39.605 --> 00:00:41.941
"Regis and Kathie Lee"
and "Regis and Kelly,"

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:44.110
he was part of all of our lives.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:46.412
He would tell funny stories
about his night out

00:00:46.412 --> 00:00:47.713
in Manhattan the night before

00:00:47.713 --> 00:00:51.418
and tell them with such
humor and class and grace.

00:00:51.418 --> 00:00:55.287
And, personally, I loved that he
never forgot his Irish roots,

00:00:55.287 --> 00:00:57.023
and as someone who grew up
in an Irish family,

00:00:57.023 --> 00:00:59.558
I could relate to
all of those stories.

00:00:59.558 --> 00:01:01.994
When I started to become famous
on "Saturday Night Live"

00:01:01.994 --> 00:01:03.430
and people would ask,

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:05.631
"What's it like when people
recognize you on the street?",

00:01:05.631 --> 00:01:08.668
I would be like,
"I feel like Regis."

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:09.969
And everyone understood that.

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:11.204
There was no need
for explanation,

00:01:11.204 --> 00:01:13.306
'cause he was
the king of New York.

00:01:13.306 --> 00:01:15.208
I was lucky enough to be on
his show as a guest,

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:17.376
and he was also on my show
numerous times.

00:01:17.376 --> 00:01:19.546
We got to know each other
pretty well.

00:01:19.546 --> 00:01:22.214
He'll be remembered as
a genuinely nice person,

00:01:22.214 --> 00:01:26.419
a funny human, a good husband,
father, and grandfather.

00:01:26.419 --> 00:01:30.623
And he always had that smile,
and when Irish eyes are smiling,

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:32.725
well, they'll steal
your heart away.

00:01:32.725 --> 00:01:35.128
Regis, we'll miss you.

